# Product Listing Page (PLP) Layout

**Description**: This rule outlines the components and architecture of the Product Listing Page (PLP). Use this rule when implementing new filtering options, modifying product card displays, working on pagination, or making any changes to how products are listed and filtered.

The PLP is structured to display product listings with filtering capabilities:

## Main Structure
- The main component is in [src/app/(product)/plp/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/(product)/plp/page.tsx)
- Contains a hero banner and product listing section
- Uses client components for interactive filtering

## Key Components
1. **PLPHeroBanner** - Category-specific header banner
2. **PLPList** - Main component for product display and filtering

## Data Fetching
- Uses server components with `async` functions
- Fetches product data from Strapi backend using filters
- Supports URL query parameters for all filters
- Builds complex query parameters for API calls

## Category Filter (Includes Children)
- When filtering by a category (e.g. کت / coat), the PLP shows **that category and all its child categories**.
- Implemented via `getCategoryAndDescendantSlugs()` in [apps/apps/frontend/src/utils/category-descendants.ts](mdc:apps/frontend/src/utils/category-descendants.ts): given a category slug and the full category tree, returns the slug plus all descendant slugs.
- The products API is called with `filters[product_main_category][Slug][$in][0]=...` etc. so Strapi returns products whose main category is the selected one or any of its children.
- Server: [plp/page.tsx](mdc:apps/frontend/src/app/(product)/plp/page.tsx) fetches all categories, resolves `categorySlugs`, and passes `allCategories` to `PLPList`. Client: [PLP/List.tsx](mdc:apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List.tsx) uses `allCategories` to resolve descendants when the user changes the category in the filter.

## Filter System
- Filter parameters:
  - Category (includes children; see above)
  - Availability (show available products only)
  - Price range (min/max)
  - Size
  - Material
  - Season
  - Gender
  - Usage
- Uses `useQueryState` from `nuqs` for state management in URL parameters
- Filters automatically trigger new API requests

## Product Display
- Products displayed in grid layout
- Each product card shows:
  - Product image
  - Category
  - Title
  - Price (with discount if applicable)
  - Rating/popularity indicators

### Product card images (performance)
- **Desktop**: Only 4 images per product are used—cover image plus 3 media for the hover overlay. The API is asked for at most 3 Media items (`populate[Media][pagination][limit]=3`); [getProductImages](apps/apps/frontend/src/utils/product.ts) caps to cover + 3. The main card shows the **cover only** (no slider); the 3 extra images appear in the hover overlay ([VariationOverlay](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/Product/CardParts/VariationOverlay.tsx)).
- **Mobile**: Only the cover image is fetched and shown ([ProductSmallCard](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/Product/SmallCard.tsx)); Media is not populated on mobile. [VirtualizedList](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/VirtualizedList.tsx) passes `includeMedia: false` when viewport is mobile.
- **No slider**: [ImageSlider](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/Product/ImageSlider.tsx) on PLP displays a single cover image only (no horizontal scroll/slider) to avoid loading many images per card.

## Responsive Components
- Desktop: Shows sidebar filter panel (280px) and product grid via [`StorefrontGrid` variant `plp`](apps/frontend/src/components/storefront/StorefrontGrid.tsx) in [`PLPDesktopList`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/PLPDesktopList.tsx)
- Mobile: Filter drawer + [`PLPMobileList`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/PLPMobileList.tsx) (`ProductSmallCard` stack)
- **Mobile filter drawer** ([`PLPListMobileFilter`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/MobileFilter.tsx)): Headless UI `Dialog` at `z-[1200]` (same as menu/search), slides from inline-start (RTL right). Do not use `--header-offset` inside the panel. Footer padding clears bottom nav (`5rem + safe-area`). Availability toggle stays in the toolbar row; pass `hideAvailability` to [`Filter`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/Filter/index.tsx) inside the drawer to avoid duplicate controls.
- Main column uses `min-w-0 flex-1` in [`PLP/List.tsx`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List.tsx) so grids do not overflow beside the sidebar

### Fluid product cards (grids)
- [`ProductCard`](apps/frontend/src/components/Product/Card.tsx): `w-full min-w-0` in grid cells; image area `aspect-[250/270]` (no fixed `md:w-[258px]`)
- [`ImageSlider`](apps/frontend/src/components/Product/ImageSlider.tsx): fills the aspect-ratio box (`h-full w-full`)

### PLP grid breakpoints (with 280px sidebar)
| Viewport | Columns |
|----------|---------|
| md (768–1023) | 2 |
| lg (1024–1279) | 2 |
| xl (1280+) | 3 |

### PLP hero banner
- [`HeroBanner`](apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/HeroBanner.tsx): full-width category image; featured mini-cards in a **stacked** grid below the banner at `xl+` only (`grid-cols-2` / `xl:grid-cols-3`), not side-by-side with a fixed 517px banner (avoids overlap at ~1280px)

## Pagination and Performance
- **API pagination**: Products are fetched one page at a time (`pagination[page]`, `pagination[pageSize]=30`). No 500-product fetch; server uses Strapi `meta.pagination` for total and pageCount.
- **Server-side sort**: Non-price sorts (e.g. `createdAt:desc`) are sent to the API (`sort[0]=...`). Price sort is applied in-memory on the current page only.
- **Deferred sidebar**: Sidebar suggestions (شاید بپسندید, تخفیف های آخرماه) are loaded in a Suspense boundary via [AsyncSidebarProducts](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List/AsyncSidebarProducts.tsx) so the main PLP content is not blocked by `getHomepageSections()`. The page passes `sidebarSlot={<Suspense><AsyncSidebarProducts /></Suspense>}` to PLPList.
- Page navigation and client-side filter changes use the same pagination (page + pageSize 30) in [PLP/List.tsx](mdc:apps/frontend/src/components/PLP/List.tsx) `fetchProducts`.

### Cache and scaling (many instances + Redis)
- PLP has **many cache keys** (every combination of category, page, sort, filters is a different URL). With many Next.js instances and a shared Redis cache handler, each instance sees only a fraction of traffic per URL, so **L1 hit rate is low** and many requests hit Redis or do a full Strapi fetch. That can make PLP feel slower after adding more instances + Redis.
- **Mitigations**: (1) `revalidate = 90` so cached responses live longer. (2) Category validation and products fetch use **internal Strapi URL** (`getStrapiServerUrl()`) on the server to avoid public TLS/DNS latency. (3) Nginx `ip_hash` for the frontend upstream so the same client tends to hit the same instance and L1 warms up. See [frontend-cache-handler.mdc](frontend-cache-handler.mdc) and [frontend-server-capacity.mdc](frontend-server-capacity.mdc).

## No Results State
- Dedicated component for when filters return no products

